
    Suppose you want to have fpmx as a local 3rd-party lib in your "proj" package.
    Suppose you want to have it placed at: proj/utils/fpmx_local

    Then:
    1) You'll have to import fpmx as:
       @@ import proj.utils.fpmx_local.prelude
       @@ require proj.utils.fpmx_local.prelude *
    2) Accordingly, in all fpmx files:
       - all inner reimports must follow the same pattern:
         @@ require proj.utils.fpmx_local.prelude.from_hyrule [->]
       - accordingly, macros one-shot-requirements must be:
         @@ hy.R.proj/utils/fpmx_local/prelude/from_hyrule.->
         (yes, hy.R uses «/» for submodules)

    This is what fpmx_local_gen (in scripts) does.
    fpmx_local.loader is modified accordingly too.

    ------------------------------------------------
        
    When running simple script (non-package) «script.hy»,
    just place fpmx_local in same folder, and importing via [³import fpmx_local.prelude⁺] will work.

